  "body": "## Why this change\n\nC194 established successful 365 mm and 375 mm edits. C195 checks whether an author can recover from an invalid collider owner while preserving the accepted 375 mm design.\n\n## Completed result\n\nBoth original authors rejected the malformed ownership relationship before native simulation, repaired the 365 mm source, preserved the accepted 375 mm source and artifacts, and regenerated that design exactly. Both passed on their first formal submission. Four author builds, four independent coordinator rebuilds, four 481-sample saved-scene replays, eight receiving paths, twenty-four Three.js poses and twelve reviewed import panels are retained. The continuous mapping bounds remain 0.074516468 and 0.116442263 mm under the unchanged 0.2 mm limit.\n\nThe exact reviewed head is 3ad887d680454faf56b82b8607dfcfd22e60ab34, tree b113aa5094212b941a39828c1a98aef1357c55cb. This published tree matches the original worker acceptance commit 0270f974. Original author history and the complete recorded evidence archive are preserved. C194 was integrated through PR #129 at cbb8499d.\n\n## Independent review and recovery\n\nThe original author audit passed 867 assertions. The continuation restored the archive and passed 5,812 recorded-only checks across 730 files without any new native build, scene resimulation, receiving execution or author trial. Acceptance-linked result, audit, visual and finalization hashes match. A fresh documentation/preservation check passed on the exact published head. Runtime, tests, common tools, workflows, torque contract and project metadata match the pre-merge main inputs. No hosted job was requested.\n\n## Limits and next task\n\nThe legacy driver and supplemental tail remain FAILED: 4,239 distinct passing methods and thirteen torque-read methods NOT RUN after the unchanged 30,000 ms setup failure. This public supplied-defect exercise establishes neither a blind study nor comparative authoring advantage, full regression or full release. Positive C195 builds used fresh stores. C196 is the separate frozen accepted-store promotion, actual-stale-revision rejection and state-readback regeneration workflow.\n\nThe previous integration lease expired and was reconciled under AGENTS.md. Current integrator c196-integration-b3a9f7 holds a verified expected-head lease; coordination issue #127. All earlier source, evidence and failures retain their meanings.",
